From f728c555186dcc37e3420b23b8c0af6b5d310167 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 14:29:36 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] fix(kanban): a pickup-stall alarm may re-place a
 listed card onto the pool queue

t_01a1d0214f3e63e8: the alarm scope (kanban_pickup_stall_repin.scope_refusal) accepted only runs_on=[machine:<X>], and kanban_move_pool refuses machine:<pool worker> without a host_reason, which no alarm path can pass (operator op fields are {runs_on, reason}; the local move passes none). With every eligible machine a pool worker, an alarm could re-place nothing.

scope_refusal now also accepts runs_on == [POOL_LABEL] while a pool machine other than the stalled one passes eligible_now (same capability/profile/slot/freshness rules); the machine:<X> form is unchanged. howto() (the alarm body), the refusal texts and the kanban_move tool description recommend ["pool:worker"] first. host_reason stays off the alarm path.

Proof: RED on b38b8d78cd: 10 new tests fail with 'runs_on must be exactly one machine:<X> label' (unit through refusal, operator_refusal via ksr.submit dry-run, and end-to-end kanban_move). GREEN: 11 files / 352 tests (pickup_stall*, pickup_alarm_placement, operator_call, operator_labels, hub_admission_pickup, quota_held, kanban_move, pool_queue, tools/test_kanban_tools). scripts/check --base origin/main ok.
